{{Quote|What do you think you're doing?''"<br />"''Excuse me?''"<br />"''You keep looking around.''"<br />"''Just trying to figure out what's going on.''"<br />"''You a part of it?''"<br />"''Part of what?''"<br />"''Don't play dumb.|The coastal defender stormtrooper and Cassian Andor|<ref name="Andor7" />}}
In [[5 BBY]], a '''coastal defender stormtrooper''' served as part of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Occupation of Niamos|occupation]] [[Imperial Military|force]] on the [[Planet|world]] [[Niamos]]. That [[Standard year|year]], he noticed the incognito [[thief]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] as the latter was heading to the [[Arkie's]] shop. Seeking to exercise his authority, the [[Coastal defender stormtrooper|trooper]] accosted Andor, treating him as if he was suspected of being affiliated with a group of [[human]]s being pursued by Imperial forces at that [[time]]. After questioning Andor, the [[Stormtrooper|trooper]] instructed a [[Unidentified KX-series security droid (Niamos)|KX-series security droid]] to watch him, and the thief was eventually transported to a [[Niamos Courthouse|courthouse]] for sentencing on various charges.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Hang onto this one for me. I wanna check the shelter.|The coastal defender stormtrooper, to a KX-series security droid on Cassian Andor|<ref name="Andor7" />}}
A [[human]]<ref name="Human" /> served as a [[coastal defender stormtrooper]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Andor7" /> by [[5 BBY]].<ref name="Date">The events of {{Andor|Announcement}}, including the appearance of the [[coastal defender stormtrooper]] on [[Niamos]], take place in [[5 BBY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''.</ref> That [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Andor7" /> he<ref name="Highlights" /> served on<ref name="Andor7" /> the [[Planet|world]]<ref name="Niamos">{{Databank|niamos|Niamos}}</ref> [[Niamos]] as part of its Imperial [[Occupation of Niamos|occupation]] [[Imperial Military|force]]. At one point, the [[stormtrooper]] was stationed on [[Pier Nine]] in front of the [[Arkie's]] shop while a pair of his fellow [[trooper]]s were pursuing a group of humans on a [[beach]]. The pursuit was noticed by the [[thief]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], who was residing on Niamos under the assumed identity "Keef Girgo" and was going to visit Arkie's. As Andor approached the venue, the coastal defender stormtrooper noticed him frequently looking around and stopped him. The trooper then began questioning Andor as to whether he was affiliated with the fleeing individuals.<ref name="Andor7" />

[[File:Pier_Nine.png|thumb|left|300px|The coastal defender stormtrooper accosted Cassian Andor on Niamos.]]
Their conversation was interrupted by the approach of the fugitives, at which point the trooper used his [[comlink]] to notify the Imperial forces of the sighting of the pursued humans. Although Andor casually offered to "wait" for the stormtrooper in case he intended to join in the pursuit, the trooper continued with the questioning as a pair of Imperial [[KX-series security droid]]s approached their position while capturing several of the fleeing humans. The trooper then called the [[Unidentified KX-series security droid (Niamos)|nearest]] [[Security droid|droid]] over for assistance with Andor. Claiming he wanted to check a shelter, the trooper instructed the [[droid]] to "hang onto" Andor for him.<ref name="Andor7" />

As the trooper then walked over to the entrance to Arkie's and joined a conversation with two other coastal defender stormtroopers, the security droid interpreted his command literally, proceeding to hold Andor aloft in a choking grip. Andor, in turn, first attempted to convince the approaching droid that the trooper had merely meant for him to "watch" over him and, when that failed, attempted to call out to the trooper in order to have him clarify his instructions and thus help resolve the situation Andor was in. Ultimately, Andor was transported to a local [[Niamos Courthouse|courthouse]], where he was sentenced to six years of [[prison]] labor for charges including "civil disruption," "anti-Imperial speech," "fleeing the scene of anti-Imperial activity," and "attempted damage to Imperial property."<ref name="Andor7" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|You look like you're sweating.''"<br />"''Well, it's hot.''"<br />"''Or you've been running.''"<br />"''Why would I be running?''"<br />"''Because you're a part of it.|The coastal defender stormtrooper and Cassian Andor|<ref name="Andor7" />}}
During his service on Niamos,<ref name="Andor7" /> the coastal defender stormtrooper sought to exercise his authority over civilians.<ref name="Highlights" /> To that end, he accosted Cassian Andor, interpreting the latter's sweating and casting glances at his surroundings as indicators that Andor was affiliated with a group of humans that Imperial forces were pursuing at the [[time]]. The trooper also aggressively treated Andor's surprised reaction as an attempt at playing innocent.<ref name="Andor7" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Pier Nine, Pier Nine, runners heading south!|The coastal defender stormtrooper, into his comlink|<ref name="Andor7" />}}
The coastal defender stormtrooper wore<ref name="Andor7" /> [[plastoid]]<ref name="R1G">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> [[shoretrooper armor]]. The trooper's [[armor]] set was similar to<ref name="Andor7" /> that of the later enlisted<ref name="R1G" /> shoretrooper [[squad leader]]s,<ref name="Hasbro">{{Hasbro|subdomain=pulse|url=news/rogue-one-star-wars-story-introduces-scarif-stormtrooper|text=Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Introduces the Scarif Stormtrooper}}</ref> but instead of a fabric [[kama]] [[Clothing|skirt]],<ref name="R1G" /> it featured<ref name="Andor7" /> plastoid faulds and a pouch for storing [[blaster gas]] cartridge magazines&mdash;two elements that it had in common with armor of shoretrooper [[captain]]s.<ref name="R1G" /> The trooper wielded a [[E-11 medium blaster rifle]] and was equipped with a comlink.<ref name="Andor7" />

==Behind the scenes==
The coastal defender stormtrooper appeared in "[[Announcement]]," the seventh episode of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''{{'s}} [[Andor Season 1|first season]],<ref name="Andor7" /> which was aired on [[October 19]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release dates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-8-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> The character, although uncredited in the episode,<ref name="Andor7" /> was voiced by<ref name="vo">{{Twitter|DavidWCollins|status/1582807719395741698|[[David W. Collins]]|date=2022-10-19|quote="#andorspoilers &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; "Are you a part of it?" A gloriously disdainful shoretrooper VO performance by @SamWitwer #Andor #voiceover #LoopGroup"|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/8L9Sm}}</ref><ref name="Witwer">{{Twitter|SamWitwer|status/1582843258228510720|[[Sam Witwer]]|date=2022-10-19|quote=Are you a part of it?|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/rElgc}}</ref> established ''[[Star Wars]]'' actor<ref name="Insider199">{{InsiderCite|199|Sam Witwer Unleashed! The Voice of Maul}}</ref> [[Sam Witwer]].<ref name="vo" /><ref name="Witwer" />

